e 3): per-call-key tabling with an immutable least fixed point (replaces the active-call guard); recursion through negation is refused before evaluation; the exact rule-head grammar is `[(name args...) body...]`. Work budget provides the execution backstop for fresh-value recursion. |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:234:| Numeric identity/arithmetic | Documented difference | Preserve the ratified CBOR identity policy and explicit unsupported-carrier refusals. |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:235:| `get-else`, `missing?` | Exact target on supported fact sources | Already index-aware special forms; edge semantics pending oracle cases. |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:236:| Deterministic aggregates | Exact target within declared numeric domain | Existing six plus additions specified below; edge cases pending. |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:237:| Finite pull | Documented-difference profile | Useful for views, but schema-free cardinality/reference/wildcard behavior is not general Datomic pull parity. |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:241:| Ambient function resolution, fulltext, randomness | Refused/deferred | Boundaries specified below. |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:259:integers or `-1`. Timeout, when supplied, is a positive integer number of\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:260:milliseconds. Until oracle verification establishes matching validation,\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:271:schema-aware Datomic pull.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:286:Source-qualified pull, dynamic patterns and other unverified forms must\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:289:Applications that require schema-dependent cardinality or reference\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:291:infer schema or turn numeric values into references automatically.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:293:### Numeric limitation\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:305:limitation from intended numeric identity.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:307:This work does not change persisted numeric identity, canonical bytes,\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:309:compatibility domain excludes numeric combinations whose behavior is\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:333:- `median`\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:343:multiplicity, variance convention, median behavior, numeric result types\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:349:`rand`, `sample`, fulltext, database-function lookup and arbitrary custom\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:557:unqualified. Do not replace the guarantee with checks at clause boundaries.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:573:unqualified source implementation. Admission inspects descriptors without\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:578:`:bounded-source-unqualified` reason and the source variable. It must\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:601:\"Admitted\" does not mean the Client oracle has verified anything: it\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:712:tests against `bt/slice` and an explicit sorted-filter oracle, including\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:843:## Conformance corpus and oracle\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:855:- `src/dev/dao/space/datomic_query_oracle.clj`\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:858:keywords, lists, numeric kinds and queries. Do not pass rich numbers\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:859:through ordinary JSON numeric decoding and lose their identity.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:867:- Evidence class, artifact/backend version and oracle provenance.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:869:  numeric tolerance.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:878:Datomic schema and transaction setup belong to its loader. DaoSpace\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:897:The oracle runner emits candidate observations to a separate output.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:909:negation/disjunction, aggregates, rules, finite pull, numeric differences\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:929:Tests must not regenerate their own oracle or corpus digest. Maintain a\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:952:| 0 — Contract and fixtures | Architect: this document. Engineer: corpus, README/errata/provenance, fixture namespace, conformance harness, oracle runner and dev-only dependency alias. | Every contract point classified; no fabricated oracle evidence; fixtures load portably; disputed behavior has explicit oracle cases; pending cases reported honestly. | 3–5 |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:956:| 2 — Deterministic language coverage | Engineer: `query.cljc`, aggregate/numeric tests and adapter tests. | Six specified aggregate capabilities added; arities and parameters preserved; empty/grouped/`:with` cases; abbreviated current-fact patterns; special-form edges; three-host numeric-domain agreement. | 6–10 |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:957:| 3 — Rules and semantic conformance | Engineer: core rules and `test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc`; corpus expansion. | Required-bound heads; left/right/mutual finite positive recursion; cycles, alternatives and unbound entry calls; immutable tabling/fixed-point correction where necessary; unsupported recursion through negation refused; fresh-value work bounded by Phase 4; existing VM rules pass. | 8–14 |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:958:| 5 — Qualification and integration | Engineer: complete conformance, counters, ownership and downstream tests. Architect: final matrix and status headers. | Supported cases verified; differences/refusals executable; read budgets hold; downstream callers pass; no remaining unverified claim inside the qualified exact domain; docs match implementation. Additionally requires evidence that Phase 4a restrictions are removed only for paths qualified by Phase 4b. | 7–11 |\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:978:- `dao.space.schema`.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:1029:oracle evidence remain absent.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:1057:host-only numeric shortcut may enter the portable path. Host exceptions\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:1059:qualified domain.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:1069:- Datomic numeric identity where it conflicts with ratified CBOR identity.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:1111:differences, oracle/backend versions and host gates.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
