{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '206,260p' test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md; sed -n '323,354p' docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md; cat docker/oracle/reconcile/probe_aggregates.clj; cat docker/oracle/reconcile/idmap_rerun.clj\"","aggregated_output":"## E15 — Phase 2 aggregate conventions and their limits\n\nFrozen DaoSpace-side conventions (Client behavior is unmeasured; every case\nis `oracle` pending):\n\n- Aggregates fold the content-distinct rows projected to the `:find`,\n  `:with` and aggregate-argument variables, so duplicates vanish unless\n  `:with` distinguishes them; `distinct` returns a set.\n- `median`: odd count -> the middle element itself (its kind kept); even\n  count -> the double mean of the two middle elements. `variance`:\n  POPULATION variance (divide by n); a single value gives 0.0; `stddev` is its\n  square root. `(min n ?x)` -> the n smallest ascending, `(max n ?x)` -> the n\n  largest descending, duplicates kept, n above the count returns everything.\n- Order statistics sort by exact numeric order across kinds with the owner's\n  tie rule (an exact operand before a float64, then the shorter canonical\n  encoding), so tied kinds order identically on every host; non-numeric\n  operands are refused (\"requires numeric operands\"), never coerced.\n- Float results are asserted for EXACT equality with no tolerance: values are\n  folded as doubles in the fixed sorted order, and `+ - * /` and `sqrt` are\n  correctly rounded IEEE-754 operations on every host. This is claimed only\n  for the integer inputs the cases use, not for arbitrary floats.\n- The kind of an INTEGRAL double result (7.0) is not host-portable: a\n  JavaScript number cannot be told from the integer 7 without a carrier, so\n  the corpus compares such results by value (`numeric-value`); the JVM kind\n  is pinned in `dao.space.query-aggregates-test`. The tie ORDER of kinds is\n  likewise pinned there, with `cbor/content=`, not in this harness.\n- A `distinct` set collapses elements the host treats as `=`: on the JVM\n  `1.0M` and `1.00M` are one member (the E1 limitation applied to a set).\n- Numeric carriers (decimals, ratios, float64 carriers) have no host\n  arithmetic on JavaScript and Dart: `variance`, `stddev` and an even-count\n  `median` refuse explicitly (\"does not accept a numeric carrier\",\n  `agg.variance-carrier-refused`, hosts `cljs` and `cljd`). The JVM evaluates\n  BigDecimal as a host number. Order statistics (odd `median`, `min`/`max`\n  with n) never do arithmetic and work with carriers everywhere. A float64\n  is a carrier on JavaScript only; a Dart double and a JVM Double are native\n  numbers. Decimals are carriers on both JavaScript and Dart. So an\n  even-count `median` over tied kinds is evaluated on `clj` and `cljd`\n  (`agg.median-tied-kinds`), refused explicitly on `cljs`\n  (`agg.median-tied-kinds-carrier-refused`), and the odd-count\n  `agg.median-tied-kinds-odd` (no arithmetic) runs on every host.\n- `rand` and `sample` remain excluded, at both layers: the core throws\n  \"Unknown aggregate in :find\", and the Datomic adapter refuses them first as\n  `:unsupported` (\"randomized aggregates are excluded from the profile\").\n- `(max n ?x)` tie order: among values that tie numerically the order is the\n  reverse of the ascending order, so a float64 precedes the exact operand\n  (`[2.0 1.0 1]`, where `(min n ?x)` gives `[1 1.0 2.0]`).\n- An aggregate argument must be a query variable: `(count [1 2])` and other\n  non-variable arguments are refused (\"aggregate argument must be a query\n  variable\"). Earlier phases parsed them and projected nil at grouping; the\n  stricter refusal was chosen over an explicit laxness note.\n\n## E14 — Syntax depth is bounded by a documented constant\n\nRecursive validation, translation and pull parsing walk query syntax by host\nrecursion. The adapter therefore refuses native query syntax (the query map or\n- `count`\n- `count-distinct`\n- `sum`\n- `min`\n- `max`\n- `avg`\n\nAdd:\n\n- `distinct`\n- `median`\n- `variance`\n- `stddev`\n- Parameterized `(min n ?x)` and `(max n ?x)`\n\nAggregate parsing must preserve parameters and validate arity. These\nadditions belong to generic core semantics, not adapter-supplied function\nclosures.\n\nFreeze empty-input results, grouping, duplicate elimination, `:with`\nmultiplicity, variance convention, median behavior, numeric result types\nand ordering/tie behavior through fixtures. Arithmetic carriers that the\nhost cannot safely evaluate remain explicit refusals. Cross-host\nfloating-point tolerances must be justified per case; do not use a\nblanket tolerance to conceal type or algorithm differences.\n\n`rand`, `sample`, fulltext, database-function lookup and arbitrary custom\naggregate resolution are excluded. Ambient randomness and global symbol\nresolution are not acceptable shortcuts. A future random aggregate\nrequires explicit entropy ownership and consumption semantics.\n\nExplicit caller function capabilities remain a DaoSpace extension.\n(require '[datomic.client.api :as d])\n(def cl (d/client {:server-type :datomic-local :storage-dir :mem :system \"probe\"}))\n(d/create-database cl {:db-name \"p\"})\n(def db (d/db (d/connect cl {:db-name \"p\"})))\n(defn q* [find vs]\n  (try (d/q {:query (list :find find :in '$ '[?v ...]) :args [db vs]})\n       (catch Throwable e (ex-message e))))\n(doseq [vs [[1 2] [3 4] [1 2 3 4] [37 40] [1.0 2.0] [1 2.0] [-3 -4] [1 2 3]]]\n  (println vs \"median ->\" (pr-str (q* '(median ?v) vs))))\n(println \"min 0 ->\" (pr-str (q* '(min 0 ?v) [3 1 2])))\n(println \"min -1 ->\" (pr-str (q* '(min -1 ?v) [3 1 2])))\n(println \"rand ->\" (pr-str (q* '(rand ?v) [3 1 2])))\n(require '[clojure.walk :as walk]\n         '[dao.space.datomic-query-fixtures :as fx]\n         '[dao.space.datomic-query-conformance-test :as ct]\n         '[dao.space.datomic-query-oracle :as o])\n(def same? @#'ct/same?)\n(def load-fixture! @#'o/load-fixture!)\n(def normalize @#'o/normalize)\n(def cfg (assoc o/datomic-local-backend :ref-attrs #{:e :person/friend :note/session}))\n(defn client-fn [s] (requiring-resolve (symbol \"datomic.client.api\" (name s))))\n(def cl ((client-fn 'client) (:client cfg)))\n(defn load-graph!\n  \"Graph nodes that only appear as values need to exist as entities: give\n   every node a :node/id so the tempid is asserted as an entity too.\"\n  [cl db-name fixture-id]\n  (let [facts (fx/fixture-facts fixture-id)\n        nodes (distinct (mapcat (fn [[a _ b]] [a b]) facts))\n        tid (fn [n] (str \"n\" n))]\n    ((client-fn 'create-database) cl {:db-name db-name})\n    (let [conn ((client-fn 'connect) cl {:db-name db-name})]\n      ((client-fn 'transact) conn\n       {:tx-data [{:db/ident :e :db/valueType :db.type/ref :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many}\n                  {:db/ident :node/id :db/valueType :db.type/long :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one}]})\n      (let [{:keys [tempids]} ((client-fn 'transact) conn\n                               {:tx-data (into (mapv (fn [n] [:db/add (tid n) :node/id n]) nodes)\n                                               (map (fn [[a _ b]] [:db/add (tid a) :e (tid b)]) facts))})]\n        {:conn conn\n         :logical->real (into {} (map (fn [n] [n (get tempids (tid n))])) nodes)}))))\n\n\n(defn run-case [id]\n  (let [c (fx/case-by-id id)\n        fids (vec (distinct (keep #(get % \"db\") (get c \"inputs\"))))\n        names (into {} (map-indexed (fn [i f] [f (str \"recon-\" id \"-\" i)])) fids)\n        dbs (into {} (map (fn [f] [f (if (= f \"graph\")\n                                                (load-graph! cl (get names f) f)\n                                                (load-fixture! cl (get names f) f (:ref-attrs cfg)))])) fids)\n        l->r (apply merge (map :logical->real (vals dbs)))\n        r->l (into {} (map (fn [[l r]] [r l])) l->r)\n        sub (fn [x] (walk/postwalk #(if (and (integer? %) (contains? l->r %)) (get l->r %) %) x))\n        args (mapv (fn [in] (if (contains? in \"db\")\n                              ((client-fn 'db) (get-in dbs [(get in \"db\") :conn]))\n                              (sub (fx/decode (get in \"value\")))))\n                   (get c \"inputs\"))\n        res (try (let [raw ((client-fn 'q) {:query (sub (fx/case-query c)) :args args})]\n                   [:result (normalize r->l raw)])\n                 (catch Throwable e [:error (str (class e)) (ex-message e)]))]\n    (doseq [f fids] (try ((client-fn 'delete-database) cl {:db-name (get names f)}) (catch Throwable _ nil)))\n    (let [exp (fx/case-expected c)\n          verdict (when (= :result (first res))\n                    (if (same? (get c \"comparison\") exp (set (second res))) :AGREE :DIFFER))]\n      (println id verdict)\n      (when (not= verdict :AGREE)\n        (println \"  exp\" (pr-str exp))\n        (println \"  obs\" (pr-str res))))))\n(doseq [id *command-line-args*] (run-case id))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'median|positive integer|parse-aggregate|agg-parameter|parameter' src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc; sed -n '1,230p' src/dev/dao/space/datomic_query_oracle.clj; sed -n '872,902p' docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'median|positive integer|parse-aggregate|agg-parameter|parameter' src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc; sed -n '1,230p' src/dev/dao/space/datomic_query_oracle.clj; sed -n '872,902p' docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md\"","aggregated_output":"test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:2:  \"Phase 2 core language coverage: the aggregates distinct, median,\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:3:   variance, stddev and parameterized (min n ?x) / (max n ?x), plus the\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:16:   - median: odd count -> the middle element itself (its kind kept); even\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:91:(deftest median-odd-even-and-grouped\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:93:    (is (= #{[3]} (qq '[:find (median ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]] scores))))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:95:    (is (= #{[3.5]} (qq '[:find (median ?v) :with ?e :where [?e :s/v ?v]] scores))))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:98:           (qq '[:find ?g (median ?v) :where [?e :s/g ?g] [?e :s/v ?v]] scores))))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:99:  (testing \"a single value is its own median\"\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:100:    (is (= #{[7]} (qq '[:find (median ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]] [[1 :s/v 7]])))))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:115:(deftest parameterized-min-and-max\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:128:  (testing \"the unparameterized forms are unchanged\"\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:132:(deftest aggregate-arity-and-parameters-are-validated\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:138:                '[:find (median 2 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:141:                '[:find (median) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:150:                '[:find (median 3) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:158:  (doseq [agg '[median variance stddev distinct]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:164:  (doseq [agg '[median variance stddev]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:173:  (let [forms ['[:find (median ?v) (variance ?v) (stddev ?v) :with ?e :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:175:               '[:find ?g (median ?v) :where [?e :s/g ?g] [?e :s/v ?v]]]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:195:  (testing \"median over [1 1 1.0 2.0] is the double mean of the middle pair (1 and 1.0)\"\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:200:    (let [even-median #(qq '[:find (median ?v) :with ?e :where [?e :k/v ?v]] ties)]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:201:      #?(:cljd (is (= #{[1.0]} (even-median)))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:202:         :clj (is (= #{[1.0]} (even-median)))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:203:         :cljs (is (re-find #\"does not accept a numeric carrier\" (refusal even-median))))))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:207:  (testing \"an odd-count median keeps the kind of the middle element\"\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:208:    (let [[[m]] (seq (qq '[:find (median ?v) :where [?e :k/v ?v]] ties))]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:232:  (testing \"median of an odd count needs no arithmetic and keeps the carrier\"\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:233:    (let [[[m]] (seq (qq '[:find (median ?v) :where [?e :d/v ?v]] decimals))]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:244:  [variance even-median]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:247:    (is (re-find #\"does not accept a numeric carrier\" (refusal even-median)))))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:252:        even-median #(qq '[:find (median ?v) :with ?e :where [?e :d/v ?v]]\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:254:    #?(:cljd (carrier-refusals variance even-median)\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:257:              (is (= #{[4.0]} (even-median)) \"mean of the middle pair 3 and 5\"))\ntest/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc:258:       :cljs (carrier-refusals variance even-median))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2306:(defn- agg-median\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2316:      (let [a (host-double 'median (nth v (dec mid)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2317:            b (host-double 'median (nth v mid))]\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2337:  \"name -> {:arities #{counts of arguments incl. parameters}, :f (fn [params\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2357:   'median {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (agg-median xs))},\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2362:(defn- parse-aggregate\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2363:  \"Parse `(name arg)` or `(min|max n arg)`: the parameters are preserved\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2365:   declared arities, and a parameter must be a positive integer.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2384:          (throw (ex-info \"aggregate parameter must be a positive integer\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2385:                          {:aggregate agg-sym, :parameter p}))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2397:        (seq? el) (parse-aggregate el)\n(ns dao.space.datomic-query-oracle\n  \"JVM-only oracle runner for the datomic-q-v1 corpus.\n\n   Executes the public `datomic.client.api/q` for oracle-eligible cases and\n   writes CANDIDATE observations to a separate output file. It never reads\n   the frozen corpus for write, never rewrites expectations, and refuses an\n   output path under test/resources. Promotion of an observation into the\n   corpus is a reviewed human step (datomic-q-v1.README.md).\n\n   The Datomic Client backend is NOT yet selected. The backend is an explicit\n   parameter: `--backend unselected` (the default) reports every eligible case\n   as a pending observation without touching any Datomic code; `--backend\n   <edn-map>` supplies a Client configuration:\n\n     {:client {:server-type :dev-local :system \\\"datomic-q-v1\\\"}\n      :db-name \\\"datomic-q-v1-oracle\\\"\n      :ref-attrs #{:person/friend :note/session}}\n\n   :client is passed to datomic.client.api/client. Each fixture gets its own\n   disposable database (created, loaded, queried, deleted). A Peer runner, a\n   mock or a DaoSpace-generated answer is never a substitute for this oracle.\n\n   Fixture loading here is independent of the DaoSpace loader. Schema is\n   derived from the logical facts: value type from the values, cardinality\n   many when one entity repeats an attribute, and :db.type/ref only for\n   attributes listed in :ref-attrs (the corpus records no schema).\n\n   `--backend datomic-local` selects Datomic Local (:server-type\n   :datomic-local, :storage-dir :mem), the owner-chosen oracle backend; the\n   observation document records the Datomic jar versions actually loaded.\n\n   Run: clj -M:oracle -m dao.space.datomic-query-oracle --backend unselected\n        clj -M:oracle -m dao.space.datomic-query-oracle --backend datomic-local\"\n  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.java.io :as io]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.space.datomic-query-fixtures :as fx]))\n\n\n(def default-output \"target/datomic-q-v1-observations.edn\")\n\n\n(def ^:private ineligible-points\n  \"Points with no Client q equivalent to execute: the internal db-first\n   arity, raw DaoSpace sources, and DaoSpace d5 views.\"\n  #{\"api.db-first-refused\" \"source.raw-refused\" \"source.daospace-values\"})\n\n\n(defn oracle-eligible?\n  [c]\n  (and (not (contains? ineligible-points (get c \"point\")))\n       (every? #(= \"facts\" (get-in (fx/fixtures) [(get % \"db\") \"view\"] \"facts\"))\n               (filter #(contains? % \"db\") (get c \"inputs\")))))\n\n\n(defn- safe-output!\n  [path]\n  (let [p (.getPath (.getCanonicalFile (io/file path)))]\n    (when (or (str/includes? p \"/test/resources/\")\n              (str/ends-with? p \"datomic-q-v1.json\"))\n      (throw (ex-info \"refusing to write observations into the frozen corpus\"\n                      {:path path})))\n    path))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Unselected backend: honest pending observations\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- pending-observation\n  [c reason]\n  {:id (get c \"id\")\n   :observation :pending\n   :reason reason\n   :api \"datomic.client.api/q\"\n   :api-version \"1.0.69\"\n   :backend :unselected})\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Selected backend: independent Datomic loader and execution\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- client-fn\n  [sym]\n  (or (requiring-resolve (symbol \"datomic.client.api\" (name sym)))\n      (throw (ex-info \"datomic.client.api is unavailable; use the :oracle alias\"\n                      {:fn sym}))))\n\n\n(defn- value-type\n  [v]\n  (cond (keyword? v) :db.type/keyword\n        (string? v) :db.type/string\n        (integer? v) :db.type/long\n        (float? v) :db.type/double\n        (decimal? v) :db.type/bigdec\n        (instance? clojure.lang.BigInt v) :db.type/bigint\n        :else (throw (ex-info \"no Datomic type for fixture value\" {:value v}))))\n\n\n(defn- schema-for\n  [facts ref-attrs]\n  (->> facts\n       (group-by second)\n       (map (fn [[a rows]]\n              (let [many? (some (fn [[_ n]] (> n 1))\n                                (frequencies (map first rows)))]\n                {:db/ident a\n                 :db/valueType (if (contains? ref-attrs a)\n                                 :db.type/ref\n                                 (value-type (nth (first rows) 2)))\n                 :db/cardinality (if many? :db.cardinality/many :db.cardinality/one)})))\n       vec))\n\n\n(defn- load-fixture!\n  \"Create a disposable database and load fixture facts under tempids.\n   Returns {:conn .. :logical->real {..}}.\"\n  [client db-name fixture-id ref-attrs]\n  (let [create (client-fn 'create-database)\n        connect (client-fn 'connect)\n        transact (client-fn 'transact)\n        facts (fx/fixture-facts fixture-id)\n        _ (create client {:db-name db-name})\n        conn (connect client {:db-name db-name})\n        _ (transact conn {:tx-data (schema-for facts ref-attrs)})\n        tempid (fn [e] (str \"e\" e))\n        data (mapv (fn [[e a v]]\n                     [:db/add (tempid e) a (if (and (contains? ref-attrs a) (integer? v))\n                                             (tempid v)\n                                             v)])\n                   facts)\n        {:keys [tempids]} (transact conn {:tx-data data})]\n    {:conn conn\n     :logical->real (into {} (map (fn [e] [e (get tempids (tempid e))]))\n                          (distinct (map first facts)))}))\n\n\n(defn- normalize\n  \"Map real entity ids back to logical ids anywhere in a result (pull\n   :db/id, reference values, tuple cells). Real ids are large allocated\n   numbers, so a plain value is never mistaken for one.\"\n  [real->logical x]\n  (cond\n    (and (integer? x) (contains? real->logical x)) (get real->logical x)\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (normalize real->logical v)])) x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv #(normalize real->logical %) x)\n    (set? x) (set (map #(normalize real->logical %) x))\n    (sequential? x) (mapv #(normalize real->logical %) x)\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn- input-value\n  \"The Client-side value of one case input: a Datomic db for a fixture, else\n   the decoded datum.\"\n  [dbs in]\n  (if (contains? in \"db\")\n    ((client-fn 'db) (get-in dbs [(get in \"db\") :conn]))\n    (fx/decode (get in \"value\"))))\n\n\n(defn- observe-selected\n  \"Execute one case through datomic.client.api/q against the configured\n   backend. Every fixture the case names gets its own disposable database,\n   deleted afterwards.\"\n  [{:keys [client db-name ref-attrs] :or {ref-attrs #{}}} c]\n  (let [cl ((client-fn 'client) client)\n        delete (client-fn 'delete-database)\n        fixture-ids (vec (distinct (keep #(get % \"db\") (get c \"inputs\"))))\n        names (into {} (map-indexed (fn [i fid] [fid (str db-name \"-\" i)])) fixture-ids)\n        base {:id (get c \"id\")\n              :api \"datomic.client.api/q\"\n              :api-version \"1.0.69\"\n              :backend client\n              :arg-map-options (fx/case-options c)}\n        error (fn [phase e]\n                (assoc base\n                       :observation :error\n                       :phase phase\n                       :error-class (.getName (class e))\n                       :message (ex-message e)\n                       :data (ex-data e)))]\n    (try\n      ;; Throwable throughout: a backend StackOverflowError is an observation\n      ;; too. A fixture Datomic cannot hold (for example one attribute with\n      ;; both long and double values) is a :fixture-load observation for\n      ;; every case that names it, not a runner failure.\n      (try\n        (let [dbs (into {} (map (fn [fid]\n                                  [fid (load-fixture! cl (get names fid) fid ref-attrs)]))\n                        fixture-ids)\n              real->logical (into {} (for [{:keys [logical->real]} (vals dbs)\n                                           [l r] logical->real]\n                                       [r l]))\n              arg-map (merge {:query (fx/case-query c)\n                              :args (mapv #(input-value dbs %) (get c \"inputs\"))}\n                             (fx/case-options c))]\n          (try\n            (let [raw ((client-fn 'q) arg-map)]\n              (assoc base\n                     :observation :result\n                     :raw raw\n                     :normalized (normalize real->logical raw)))\n            (catch Throwable e (error :query e))))\n        (catch Throwable e (error :fixture-load e)))\n      (finally\n        (doseq [fid fixture-ids]\n          (try (delete cl {:db-name (get names fid)})\n               (catch Exception _ nil)))))))\n\n\n(defn- jar-versions\n  \"Versions of the Datomic jars actually on the classpath, so an observation\n   file records what ran rather than what was requested.\"\n  []\n  (into (sorted-map)\n        (keep (fn [p]\n                (when-let [[_ a v] (re-find #\"/com/datomic/([^/]+)/([^/]+)/[^/]+\\.jar$\" p)]\n                  [a v])))\n        (str/split (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\") #\":\")))\n\n\n(defn run\n  \"Observe every eligible case (or the one named by :only). Returns the\n   candidate-observation document. Never writes.\"\n  [{:keys [backend only]}]\n  (let [cases (cond->> (fx/cases) only (filter #(= only (get % \"id\"))))\n        eligible (filter oracle-eligible? cases)\n        skipped (remove oracle-eligible? cases)]\nAn unverified expectation is not a passing conformance assertion.\nInvented expected answers must not be attributed to Datomic.\n\n### Dual loaders\n\nOne logical fixture has independent Datomic and DaoSpace loaders.\nDatomic schema and transaction setup belong to its loader. DaoSpace\nexplicit fact/current-view construction belongs to its loader.\n\nNormalize allocated entity IDs through fixture identity mappings,\nincluding IDs embedded in pull results and references. Do not normalize\naway semantic differences such as cardinality or missing values.\nTransaction IDs require separate explicit semantics and are outside the\ninitial accepted history domain.\n\n### Oracle\n\nExecute public `datomic.client.api/q` against an identified real Client\nbackend. Client API availability alone is not a backend.\n\nRecord API version, backend kind/version, fixture identity, query/options,\nnormalization procedure and observed result/error. Use an explicit\ndisposable fixture database. A Peer-only runner may supply additional\nlanguage evidence but cannot certify Client behavior.\n\nThe oracle runner emits candidate observations to a separate output.\nIt must never rewrite frozen expected values as part of a test run.\nCorpus promotion requires review.\n\nIf the backend cannot run, preserve the unverified status and report the\nmissing evidence. Do not qualify the release using wrapper source,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"U1 is a convention difference, not a CBOR identity conflict. I’ll retain the pinned median behavior, accept non-positive integer limits for parameterized min/max, and document U3 as a schema difference. Two promotion safeguards also need to be explicit: ID mapping must not rewrite ordinary numeric values, and U3’s schema error does not establish empty-input aggregate behavior.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2300,2390p' src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc; sed -n '132,165p' test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.json'\nx=json.load(open(p))\nprint(type(x).__name__)\ncs=x.get('cases',[]) if isinstance(x,dict) else x\nfor c in cs:\n if c.get('id') in ['agg.empty-input','in.empty-source','ambient.fulltext-refused','agg.parameter-not-positive','agg.median-with-multiplicity']:\n  print(json.dumps(c,indent=2))\nPY\n\ndate -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'; TZ=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2300,2390p' src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc; sed -n '132,165p' test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.json'\nx=json.load(open(p))\nprint(type(x).__name__)\ncs=x.get('cases',[]) if isinstance(x,dict) else x\nfor c in cs:\n if c.get('id') in ['agg.empty-input','in.empty-source','ambient.fulltext-refused','agg.parameter-not-positive','agg.median-with-multiplicity']:\n  print(json.dumps(c,indent=2))\nPY\n\ndate -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'; TZ=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh'\"","aggregated_output":"  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (dart-math/sqrt x)\n     :clj (Math/sqrt x)\n     :cljs (js/Math.sqrt x)))\n\n\n(defn- agg-median\n  \"Median of numeric values: sort by `numeric-order`; an odd count answers\n   the middle element itself (its kind preserved); an even count answers the\n   double mean of the two middle elements.\"\n  [xs]\n  (let [v (sorted-numeric xs)\n        n (count v)\n        mid (quot n 2)]\n    (if (odd? n)\n      (nth v mid)\n      (let [a (host-double 'median (nth v (dec mid)))\n            b (host-double 'median (nth v mid))]\n        (/ (+ a b) 2.0)))))\n\n\n(defn- agg-variance\n  \"POPULATION variance (the sum of squared deviations from the mean divided\n   by n), a double. Values are converted to doubles and folded in `numeric-order`\n   so the evaluation order, and therefore every IEEE-754 rounding step, is\n   fixed: addition, subtraction, multiplication and division are correctly\n   rounded on every host, so the result is the same double on all of them for\n   the same inputs. A single value has variance 0.0.\"\n  [xs]\n  (let [ds (mapv #(host-double 'variance %) (sorted-numeric xs))\n        n (count ds)\n        mean (/ (reduce + 0.0 ds) n)\n        ss (reduce (fn [acc d] (let [e (- d mean)] (+ acc (* e e)))) 0.0 ds)]\n    (/ ss n)))\n\n\n(def ^:private aggregate-fns\n  \"name -> {:arities #{counts of arguments incl. parameters}, :f (fn [params\n   xs])}. `params` are the literal leading arguments (only min and max take\n   one: the positive count n).\"\n  {'count {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (count xs))},\n   'count-distinct {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (count (content-distinct xs)))},\n   'sum {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (reduce (host-arithmetic 'sum +) 0 xs))},\n   'min {:arities #{1 2},\n         :f (fn [[n] xs]\n              (if n\n                (vec (take n (sorted-numeric xs)))\n                (reduce portable-min xs)))},\n   'max {:arities #{1 2},\n         :f (fn [[n] xs]\n              (if n\n                (vec (take n (reverse (sorted-numeric xs))))\n                (reduce portable-max xs)))},\n   'avg {:arities #{1},\n         :f (fn [_ xs]\n              (double (/ (reduce (host-arithmetic 'avg +) 0 xs) (count xs))))},\n   'distinct {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (set (content-distinct xs)))},\n   'median {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (agg-median xs))},\n   'variance {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (agg-variance xs))},\n   'stddev {:arities #{1}, :f (fn [_ xs] (sqrt-double (agg-variance xs)))}})\n\n\n(defn- parse-aggregate\n  \"Parse `(name arg)` or `(min|max n arg)`: the parameters are preserved\n   (the leading literals), the arity validated against the aggregate's\n   declared arities, and a parameter must be a positive integer.\"\n  [el]\n  (let [[agg-sym & args] el\n        spec (get aggregate-fns agg-sym)]\n    (when-not spec\n      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown aggregate in :find\" {:aggregate agg-sym})))\n    (when-not (contains? (:arities spec) (count args))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Aggregate arity does not match its definition\"\n                      {:aggregate agg-sym, :arity (count args)})))\n    (let [arg (last args)\n          params (vec (butlast args))]\n      (when (and (seq? arg) (= 'pull (first arg)))\n        (throw (ex-info \"pull cannot be used as an aggregate argument\"\n                        {:element el})))\n      (when-not (symbol? arg)\n        (throw (ex-info \"aggregate argument must be a query variable\"\n                        {:aggregate agg-sym})))\n      (doseq [p params]\n        (when-not (and (integer? p) (pos? p))\n          (throw (ex-info \"aggregate parameter must be a positive integer\"\n                          {:aggregate agg-sym, :parameter p}))))\n      {:agg (fn [xs] ((:f spec) params xs)), :arg arg, :agg-name agg-sym, :agg-params params})))\n\n\n(defn- parse-find-element\n  [el]\n(deftest aggregate-arity-and-parameters-are-validated\n  (doseq [form ['[:find (min 0 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (min -1 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (min 1.5 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (min :a ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (min 1 2 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (median 2 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (distinct 2 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (count 2 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (median) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]]]\n    (is (some? (refusal #(qq form scores))) (pr-str form)))\n  (testing \"rand and sample are not aggregates here\"\n    (is (re-find #\"Unknown aggregate\" (refusal #(qq '[:find (rand ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]] scores))))\n    (is (re-find #\"Unknown aggregate\" (refusal #(qq '[:find (sample 2 ?v) :where [?e :s/v ?v]] scores))))))\n\n\n(deftest an-aggregate-argument-must-be-a-query-variable\n  (doseq [form ['[:find (count [1 2]) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (median 3) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (min 2 [1]) :where [?e :s/v ?v]]\n                '[:find (distinct \"x\") :where [?e :s/v ?v]]]]\n    (is (refused-with? #(qq form scores) #\"aggregate argument must be a query variable\")\n        (pr-str form))))\n\n\n(deftest aggregates-over-empty-input-produce-no-row\n  (doseq [agg '[median variance stddev distinct]]\n    (is (= #{} (qq [:find (list agg '?v) :where '[?e :s/none ?v]] scores)) (str agg)))\n  (is (= #{} (qq '[:find (min 2 ?v) :where [?e :s/none ?v]] scores))))\n\n\n(deftest non-numeric-operands-are-refused-not-coerced\n  (doseq [agg '[median variance stddev]]\n    (is (re-find #\"requires numeric operands\"\ndict\n{\n  \"id\": \"in.empty-source\",\n  \"point\": \"in.ordered-args-default-source\",\n  \"workload\": null,\n  \"note\": null,\n  \"query\": [\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"find\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"sym\": \"?e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"where\"\n    },\n    [\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"?e\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kw\": \"person/name\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"_\"\n      }\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"db\": \"empty\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"options\": null,\n  \"classification\": \"exact-target\",\n  \"evidence\": \"local-dao-source\",\n  \"status\": \"executable\",\n  \"expect\": {\n    \"kind\": \"value\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"set\": []\n    }\n  },\n  \"daospace-observed\": null,\n  \"comparison\": \"exact\",\n  \"hosts\": [\n    \"clj\",\n    \"cljs\",\n    \"cljd\"\n  ],\n  \"oracle\": \"pending\",\n  \"limitation\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"ambient.fulltext-refused\",\n  \"point\": \"ambient.refused\",\n  \"workload\": null,\n  \"note\": null,\n  \"query\": [\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"find\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"sym\": \"?e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"where\"\n    },\n    [\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"?e\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kw\": \"person/name\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"_\"\n      }\n    ],\n    [\n      {\n        \"list\": [\n          {\n            \"sym\": \"fulltext\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"sym\": \"$\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kw\": \"person/name\"\n          },\n          \"Ada\"\n        ]\n      },\n      [\n        [\n          {\n            \"sym\": \"?x\"\n          }\n        ]\n      ]\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"db\": \"people\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"options\": null,\n  \"classification\": \"refused\",\n  \"evidence\": \"local-dao-source\",\n  \"status\": \"refusal\",\n  \"expect\": {\n    \"kind\": \"refusal\",\n    \"message-contains\": \"Unknown query fn\"\n  },\n  \"daospace-observed\": null,\n  \"comparison\": \"exact\",\n  \"hosts\": [\n    \"clj\",\n    \"cljs\",\n    \"cljd\"\n  ],\n  \"oracle\": \"pending\",\n  \"limitation\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"agg.empty-input\",\n  \"point\": \"aggregates.existing\",\n  \"workload\": null,\n  \"note\": \"DaoSpace returns no row for an aggregate over empty input\",\n  \"query\": [\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"find\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"list\": [\n        {\n          \"sym\": \"count\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"sym\": \"?e\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"where\"\n    },\n    [\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"?e\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kw\": \"person/nothing\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"_\"\n      }\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"db\": \"people\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"options\": null,\n  \"classification\": \"unverified\",\n  \"evidence\": \"local-dao-source\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"expect\": {\n    \"kind\": \"pending\",\n    \"reason\": \"Datomic empty-input aggregate behavior is unmeasured\"\n  },\n  \"daospace-observed\": {\n    \"kind\": \"value\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"set\": []\n    }\n  },\n  \"comparison\": \"exact\",\n  \"hosts\": [\n    \"clj\",\n    \"cljs\",\n    \"cljd\"\n  ],\n  \"oracle\": \"pending\",\n  \"limitation\": \"E7\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"agg.median-with-multiplicity\",\n  \"point\": \"aggregates.additions\",\n  \"workload\": null,\n  \"note\": \"six rows [1 2 3 4 4 10]: the mean of 3 and 4\",\n  \"query\": [\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"find\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"list\": [\n        {\n          \"sym\": \"median\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"sym\": \"?v\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"with\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"sym\": \"?e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"where\"\n    },\n    [\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"?e\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kw\": \"s/v\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"?v\"\n      }\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"db\": \"scores\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"options\": null,\n  \"classification\": \"exact-target\",\n  \"evidence\": \"local-dao-source\",\n  \"status\": \"executable\",\n  \"expect\": {\n    \"kind\": \"value\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"set\": [\n        [\n          {\n            \"float64-bits\": \"400c000000000000\"\n          }\n        ]\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"daospace-observed\": null,\n  \"comparison\": \"numeric-value\",\n  \"hosts\": [\n    \"clj\",\n    \"cljs\",\n    \"cljd\"\n  ],\n  \"oracle\": \"pending\",\n  \"limitation\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"agg.parameter-not-positive\",\n  \"point\": \"aggregates.additions\",\n  \"workload\": null,\n  \"note\": null,\n  \"query\": [\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"find\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"list\": [\n        {\n          \"sym\": \"min\"\n        },\n        0,\n        {\n          \"sym\": \"?a\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"kw\": \"where\"\n    },\n    [\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"?e\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kw\": \"person/age\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"sym\": \"?a\"\n      }\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"db\": \"people\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"options\": null,\n  \"classification\": \"refused\",\n  \"evidence\": \"local-dao-source\",\n  \"status\": \"refusal\",\n  \"expect\": {\n    \"kind\": \"refusal\",\n    \"message-contains\": \"positive integer\"\n  },\n  \"daospace-observed\": null,\n  \"comparison\": \"exact\",\n  \"hosts\": [\n    \"clj\",\n    \"cljs\",\n    \"cljd\"\n  ],\n  \"oracle\": \"pending\",\n  \"limitation\": null\n}\n2026-10-27 09:45:13 GMT\n2026-10-27 16:45:13 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-27 09:45:13 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-27 16:45:13 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a16d38-d4fc-7253-8098-51e80bd692b9\n\nReviewed the reconciliation, probe scripts, runner, E15, and aggregate implementation at `datomic-q-p5-ci@e4eed5f5`. These are convention rulings for the promotion round, not final qualification sign-off. No files changed.\n\n**U1 — retain DaoSpace’s median convention; document the difference.**\n\nChoose **(a)**. Odd counts retain the middle operand; even counts return the double mean within the existing supported arithmetic domain. Preserve the current carrier refusals and kind ordering.\n\nThis is a deliberate convention choice, **not a consequence of CBOR identity**. Matching the observed Datomic behavior would be architecturally possible, but would replace an already-pinned, portable arithmetic convention with backend-specific truncation and mixed-kind failures. The compatibility cost must be explicit.\n\nTranscribe into E15 and the aggregate contract:\n\n> Median is a documented difference. DaoSpace preserves the middle operand for odd counts and computes the double mean of the middle pair for even counts, subject to its existing arithmetic-carrier restrictions. Datomic Local 1.0.301 observations include `[1 2 3 4 4 10] → 3`, versus DaoSpace `3.5`; `[1.0 2.0] → 1.0`, versus DaoSpace `1.5`; and a mixed `[1 2.0]` refusal. These observations do not redefine DaoSpace’s convention or establish behavior for unmeasured numeric domains.\n\nReclassify `agg.median-with-multiplicity` as a documented difference, retaining its DaoSpace expectation. Preserve individual agreements under their declared comparator; they must not imply general median parity. Record result-kind differences separately where `numeric-value` comparison hides them.\n\n**U2 — accept non-positive integer parameters and return an empty aggregate collection.**\n\nChoose **(b)**. Unlike U1, the positive-only restriction contributes no required numeric or architectural guarantee. Removing it improves compatibility without changing any previously successful positive-parameter result.\n\nNormative replacement:\n\n> Parameterized `(min n ?x)` and `(max n ?x)` accept integer parameters within the supported parameter domain. For an existing aggregate group, `n <= 0` produces an empty vector; positive parameters retain the established ordering, multiplicity, and tie rules. Non-integer parameters and invalid arities remain refusals. This does not bypass query evaluation, source admission, or execution accounting.\n\nImplement this in the generic aggregate core, not through adapter query rewriting. An empty aggregate value occupies its normal result cell; it does **not** mean an empty result relation. This ruling does not settle aggregation over zero input rows.\n\nBefore promotion:\n\n- Replace the zero/negative refusal pins with result assertions.\n- Add grouped and ungrouped tests for both `min` and `max`, preserving positive and invalid-parameter coverage.\n- Measure `max 0` and `max -1` through the oracle before claiming their parity; the supplied observations establish only `min`.\n- Update E15, parameter-validation documentation, corpus provenance, and digest; run the three-host affected suites.\n\n**U3 — retain schema-free behavior; add an explicit documented-difference row.**\n\nTranscribe into the supported-domain table:\n\n| Contract point | Classification | Boundary |\n|---|---|---|\n| Attribute identifier absent from Datomic schema | Documented difference | DaoSpace fact matching requires no attribute-schema declaration: an unmatched attribute yields no bindings. The observed Datomic backend refuses unresolved attribute identifiers with `:db.error/not-an-entity`. DaoSpace does not infer or consult a schema solely to reproduce that refusal. |\n\nDo not add schema ownership or schema lookup to this adapter.\n\nThe current observations for `agg.empty-input` and `in.empty-source` establish this schema difference. **They do not establish Datomic’s empty-input aggregate behavior.** Preserve those observations, then add separate oracle cases with declared attributes but no matching facts. Empty-input aggregate parity must remain unverified until those cases execute.\n\n**Carry-forward rulings**\n\n1. **Land the runner’s identity correction before promoting the ten rerun cases.** Then obtain observations from the corrected production runner. The exploratory script’s blanket replacement of every matching integer is unsuitable as the general mechanism: it can rewrite an ordinary numeric value or aggregate parameter that happens to equal a logical entity ID. Use explicit, source-scoped fixture/case identity annotations or enumerated substitution positions. Pin a collision test demonstrating that ordinary numbers remain unchanged. Record graph reference loading and value-only node materialization in loader provenance.\n\n2. **Defer fulltext oracle qualification to a future fulltext profile.** Fulltext remains excluded from this release. Keep `ambient.fulltext-refused` as an executable DaoSpace refusal, with the Datomic observation marked inconclusive. The current compiler error proves neither equivalent refusal nor successful fulltext support. A future measurement needs a fulltext-enabled fixture and a valid backend-supported query; it is not a prerequisite for qualifying the present exclusion.\n\n3. **Keep evidence promotion precise.** Preserve historical observations and identify superseding runner versions and corpus digests. “Oracle executed” must remain distinct from “agreement,” “documented difference,” and “inconclusive.” The final qualified claim must name these boundaries and exclude unresolved cases from its exact domain."}}
